        "The route returns { content: string, cached: boolean } as JSON — the server's JSON serialisation is handled by the existing response pipeline in server.ts (same as all other handlers).",
        "107 pre-existing test failures exist in project-detail-auto-update.test.ts and project-detail-poll-modes.test.ts (all WP-005 tests failing on API.getRepo is not a function). These are the unimplemented frontend tests for the BLOCKED WP-005 and are not caused by this WP.",
        "npm run build passes cleanly. The gui/*.ts files are executed via tsx at runtime (not compiled by tsc) — tsx validates types on load.",
        "The best-effort writeFile catch block uses an empty catch (no binding) which is TypeScript 4+ compatible."
      ]
    },
    {
      "from_agent": "QA",
      "to_agent": "Security Auditor",
      "timestamp": "2026-07-24T08:51:05Z",
      "notes": [
        "All 7 AC verified via 29 new integration tests — all pass.",
        "107 pre-existing WP-005 failures (API.getRepo is not a function in project-detail-auto-update and project-detail-poll-modes) remain and are unrelated to this WP.",
        "3 pre-existing failures in repository-context.test.ts (insight deduplication) are also unrelated.",
        "New test file: tests/gui/api-chunk-text.test.ts (29 tests, all passing).",
        "npm run build passes cleanly. No regressions in any WP-004-adjacent test file.",
        "AC-4 (write error swallowing) verified structurally — the bare catch block in handleGetChunkText is present and contains no rethrow."
      ]
    },
    {
      "from_agent": "Security Auditor",
      "to_agent": "Reviewer",
      "timestamp": "2026-07-24T08:53:40Z",
      "notes": [
        "Security audit PASS — 0 Critical, 0 High findings. Two Medium observations recorded (swallowed-write-error observability gap; log injection hardening for filename in warn messages) — neither blocks approval. Two Low observations (no filename length cap on CHUNK_FILENAME_RE stem; theoretical symlink race requiring local fs write access). All 7 AC confirmed met. Recommend addressing the Medium-priority console.warn hardening (log injection via unsanitized filename) in a future cleanup pass. Ready for code review."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "claimed": false
}

